 "assumptions": [
  "Answers and error bars are the audit's out-of-scene predictions of the feature model (numeric.csv, kind sigma): mu is the predicted bias of e = value - reference, half90 the half-width of the split-conformal 90 % interval [mu - half90, mu + half90] for e, so the interval for the reference is [c - half90, c + half90] with c = value - mu. Nothing is refitted.",
  "Truth is the reference value value - e. A decision with c exactly at the threshold (infinite score) is never accepted.",
  "Calibration decisions for a test scene come from scenes outside its fold (per question type, the audit's folds, recomputed and checked against folds.csv where recorded). They are those scenes' own out-of-scene test predictions: the audit did not save its leave-two-out calibration predictions, so a calibration decision's mu and sigma come from a model whose training data included the test scene's fold, and its half90 from a conformal quantile whose calibration scores included that fold. The test scene's own answers never calibrate it, but the Learn-then-Test certificate is approximate in this respect.",
  "Learn-then-Test is the audit's procedure and settings (fixed-sequence binomial tests on a geometric grid; min_accept 30, min_accept_frac 0.05). Items are treated as independent and scenes as exchangeable, as in the audit; Wilson intervals and binomial bounds are optimistic for items that share a scene, so the scene-cluster bootstrap interval is reported too.",
  "Calibration pool 'labeller' (default) pools all of a labeller's decisions of one analysis (question types and thresholds; sweep: per |u|, both signs; margins: per decision), as the audit's gate pools question types: the certificate is on the pooled wrong-decision rate, and a per-type or per-threshold row may exceed epsilon. Pool 'family' calibrates each question type and threshold separately.",
  "The fixed-tolerance gate is taken from gate.csv as the audit ran it (kind sigma, tau_scale 1, decision accept); in an audit with several depth sources its threshold was certified on all sources together.",
  "The sweep places t = ref (1 + u) relative to the reference: an analysis device (t depends on the unknown reference), not a deployable decision. Its truth is u < 0; answers with ref <= 0 are left out.",
  "Safety decisions are one-sided: only outside calls (c > t) can be accepted, with score half90 / (c - t); an accepted call is wrong when ref <= t. The no-check baseline accepts every outside call.",
  "Margins: unordered pairs of answers of one question type in one view (dataset, scene, camera, frame) about two different single-referent objects (referents from the label folder's qa_oracle.jsonl, found by the audit's recorded checksums), oriented by question id (hashes: unrelated to the values). Direct calibration is split conformal on |e_m - (mu_A - mu_B)| / sqrt(sigma_A^2 + sigma_B^2) over pairs of the same question type outside the test scene's fold, with the same calibration caveat as above."
 ],
